      "agent": "auto",
      "prompt": "Wire the busy markers from tools/busy-marker.mjs into tools/swarm.mjs. (1) In main() (near the top, where argv is read): find the verb the way verbOf does in tools/live-processes.mjs (first word that is not an option, skipping the value after --root). If the verb is in BUSY_MARKER_VERBS, call writeBusyMarker({command: argv.join(' ') cut to 160 chars, root: the resolved root as main already computes it for the journal}) before mainInner runs, and call the returned remove() in the existing finally block. Also register a process.on('exit') handler that removes the marker file synchronously (fs.unlinkSync inside try/catch) so a crash or SIGINT does not leave one behind; a dead pid is ignored by liveBusyMarkers anyway. Marker writing must never make the command fail: wrap it in try/catch and carry on. Use dynamic import or the existing static import style of the file, whichever matches. (2) In the update command (the block that refuses with update-refused while work is running, around the runningSwarmCommands check): when not --force, also call liveBusyMarkers() and refuse with the same update-refused message style listing each marker as '  process PID  COMMAND  (ROOT)' if any are live and their pid is not this process. --force still skips both checks. Keep the existing ps-based check unchanged. (3) Write tests/update-busy-marker.test.mjs (node:test, style of tests/update.test.mjs): point the marker directory at a temp dir through the same env override busyDir uses, then run the real tools/swarm.mjs update as a child process with that env, in a way that stops before touching any install (the refusal happens before the install is looked at; for the --force case only assert that the refusal text is absent or use a case that fails fast without moving anything, never let the test update a real install): a live marker (pid of the test process) makes update print update-refused and exit non-zero; a marker with a dead pid does not block (no update-refused text); --force does not refuse over a live marker. Also add a test that a swarm command in BUSY_MARKER_VERBS writes a marker while running and removes it on exit if that can be done cheaply and deterministically (for example the validate-free path of a short command); skip that one if it would be flaky. Do not edit any other files. Many existing tests import tools/swarm.mjs; the change is additive (a best-effort marker plus one extra refusal) so the tests listed in ignoreTests are knowingly left uncovered: do not edit or run them.",
